Phasmid: canvas readback

What:     getImageData, toDataURL, toBlob and OffscreenCanvas.convertToBlob of
          2D and bitmaprenderer canvases apply one local, idempotent function
          keyed from the seed: one least significant bit of a pixel that
          blends its neighbours, only inside the region last written by
          anti-aliased or blending rasterization. putImageData, pixel-aligned
          solid fillRect and clearRect, and 1:1 drawImage of decoded images
          read back exactly. Nothing on screen changes. Off without
          canvas.noise.
Why:      Breaks cross-profile canvas linking without per-call randomness or
          a readback-relative key, agreeing across exits, sub-rectangles,
          round trips and contexts.
Profile:  canvas.noise, seed
Hooks:    third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/html_canvas_element.cc
          (ToDataURLInternal, toBlob); core/offscreencanvas/offscreen_canvas.cc
          (convertToBlob); new core/html/canvas/phasmid_readback_noise.{h,cc}
          and test; modules/canvas/canvas2d/base_rendering_context_2d.cc
          (getImageDataInternal, putImageData);
          canvas_2d_recorder_context.{h,cc} (fillRect, clearRect, drawImage,
          ResetInternal); canvas_rendering_context_2d.cc and
          offscreen_canvas_rendering_context_2d.cc (WillDraw); new
          canvas2d/phasmid_readback_provenance.{h,cc};
          modules/modules_initializer.cc (Initialize)
Contexts: main, iframe, worker, shared worker, service worker, offscreen
Guard:    tests/guards/graphics/canvas-readback.py

